sections.wikitext:
"Torn Between Two Lovers" reached No. 1 on the [[Billboard Hot 100|U.S. pop chart]] in February 1977 and achieved the same position on the [[Adult Contemporary (chart)|Easy Listening chart]] in the final week of 1976 and first week of 1977.<ref>{{cite book |title= Top Adult Contemporary: 1961-2001|last=Whitburn |first=Joel |author-link=Joel Whitburn |year=2002 |publisher=Record Research |page=152}}</ref> It remained in the ''Billboard'' top 10 for ten weeks,<ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://top40weekly.com/1977-all-charts/|title=All US Top 40 Singles For 1977|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref> and was ranked as the [[Billboard Year-End Hot 100 singles of 1977|No. 10 song for 1977]]. It also hit No. 1 on the Canadian charts, and peaked at No. 3 on the country charts of both nations.<ref>{{cite book |title= The Billboard Book Of Top 40 Country Hits: 1944-2006, Second edition|last=Whitburn |first=Joel |author-link=Joel Whitburn |year=2004 |publisher=Record Research |page=211}}</ref> In March 1977, it was No. 4 in the [[UK Singles Chart|United Kingdom]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.officialcharts.com/artist/_/mary%20macgregor/ |title=MARY MACGREGOR &#124; full Official Chart History &#124; Official Charts Company |website=Officialcharts.com |date= |accessdate=2016-10-11}}</ref>

